usage: harness [-h]
               {serve,desktop,verify,apply,continue,offer,defer,ledger,models,bench,lint-claims,capabilities,spend,rankings,trust,dogfood} ...

Cost-bounded multi-model verification & coding harness with AI sovereignty.

positional arguments:
  {serve,desktop,verify,apply,continue,offer,defer,ledger,models,bench,lint-claims,capabilities,spend,rankings,trust,dogfood}
    serve               Local web UI + JSON API over the core (loopback;
                        --auth-token optional, HARNESS_UI_AUTH_TOKEN)
    desktop             Native desktop window over the same web UI (pywebview;
                        browser fallback)
    verify              Panel + judge verification (back-compat with
                        fusion_lite.py)
    apply               Scoped code edit with a verification loop + consent
                        continuation
    continue            Continue a deferred/incomplete apply task
    offer               Ask a model for consent on a work item
    defer               Record a mid-task deferral / consent revocation
    ledger              Autonomy ledger
    models              List live free OpenRouter models (refreshed)
    bench               Run a manifest of known-answer tasks through the free
                        tier
    lint-claims         Lint a claims manifest against its quoted source
                        (hermetic: no network)
    capabilities        Model capability profiles + reliability (hypothesis
                        from /models, corrected by observed evidence)
    spend               Key identity & spend status
    rankings            Daily OpenRouter rankings: top models, climbers, and
                        evidence-driven pool-candidate proposals
    trust               Trust & correctness standing from ledger history
                        (read-only: no key, no network)
    dogfood             Self-hosting loop: ground -> live panel verify ->
                        gated self-apply (exit 0 only if every phase proved
                        its claim)

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
